  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia - Blue Leaf Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jagua is an exotic fruit that grows in the rainforests of Colombia. Products derived from the fruits (i.e. juice or powder) can be used to create temporary tattoos that disappear after two weeks. The market is growing, but also fragmented and inefficient. Currently, supply is unreliable and the shelf life is limited. Therefore, the production must shift from Jagua juice-based products towards Jagua powder-based products.Research is required, which Jagua Henna cannot afford itself (it is a start-up company) and where they also get nothing from regular financiers. In addition, this project also serves as a preparation for possible future financing, in order to scale up the overall business and value chain. The investment contributes to a sustainable, integrated value chain that in turn contributes to local employment, sustainable production and the introduction of a safe cosmetic product in the Netherlands / EU (and beyond in the long term).When the project is successful, future local investments will also be made in production capacity to enable dehydration and sourcing on a larger scale. This in turn creates local jobs.</narrative>
  </description>
